# LinkedIn returns HTTP 999 to every automated client as an anti-scraping
# measure; the profile resolves normally in a browser.
https://www\.linkedin\.com/.*

# www.fsf.org negotiates only DHE key-exchange cipher suites and rejects ECDHE
# with a handshake_failure; lychee's rustls backend implements no DHE, so the
# handshake can never complete. The page itself serves 200 (verified via curl).
https://www\.fsf\.org/.*
